{#
    The notice "you are talking with an AI" (article 50(1) of the EU AI Act), for the interface of a
    module that lets a customer or a visitor talk with an AI (a chat, an assistant).

    Include it once, ABOVE the first message:

        <twig:Molecules:AiNotice:Base usage="mymodule.chat" />

    @prop usage  string       Identifier of the usage the module declared with #[AsAiUsage] (transparency: interactive)
    @prop locale string|null  Language of the notice; defaults to the one of the request, then of the shop

    The theme holds no compliance logic and no setting: whether a notice is due, and its text in the
    current language, come from the Thelia core (ai_transparency_notice). It renders nothing when the usage
    is not interactive, is inactive, or when the merchant turned its notice off. An identifier the core does
    not know throws, so a typo is not a silent missing notice. Extra attributes (class, id) go on the
    notice; it is a polite live region, so a screen reader announces it when it is inserted.
#}
{% props usage, locale = null %}

{% set notice = ai_transparency_notice(usage, locale) %}

{% if notice is not empty %}
    {# The core escapes at output; the SnackBar prints its text raw, so the text is escaped here. #}
    {{ component('Molecules:SnackBar:Base', {
        variant: 'informative',
        withIcon: true,
        text: notice|e,
        role: 'status',
    }|merge(attributes.all)) }}
{% endif %}
